{
  "description": "Executor.governance_state() \u2014 configured vs. actually wired (PROTOCOL_SPEC 6.6.5). `acl != null` means an ACL object is attached, NOT that ACL evaluation runs: the gates are pipeline steps, and the `internal` / `testing` / `minimal` presets remove them. Every field, the derived flag included, MUST be identical across the three SDKs for every case. The accessor is a pure read \u2014 a case that changes executor state has been driven wrong. v1.16.0: the approval half of the derived flag requires all_control_modules_require_approval, because approval_gate is per-module conditional while acl_check is not \u2014 see PROTOCOL_SPEC 6.6.5.1.1.",
  "driver_contract": {
    "path": "MUST call the real accessor on a real Executor whose strategy, ACL, handler and policy were set through the public API. Reconstructing the eight booleans in the driver asserts the driver's arithmetic, not the SDK's.",
    "derived_flag_is_asserted_not_recomputed": "`expected.unprotected_control_surface` MUST be compared against what the SDK returned. A driver that recomputes it from the other seven fields is green against an implementation that never computes it at all.",
    "the_lookalike_case_is_the_point": "`custom_step_named_acl_check_is_not_the_builtin` requires registering a strategy containing a step whose NAME is `acl_check` and whose TYPE is not the built-in gate. A driver that skips it because building one is awkward has removed the only case that distinguishes a type test from a name test.",
    "purity": "After each case the driver MUST call governance_state() twice and assert both returns are equal, and MUST assert no warning was emitted and no exception raised. 6.6.5.3 forbids the accessor from enforcing, warning, throwing or mutating.",
    "liveness": "For at least one case the driver MUST call the accessor, mutate the executor (attach an ACL or swap the strategy), and call again \u2014 the second result MUST reflect the change. A cached value passes every static case.",
    "approval_gate_is_conditional": "The driver MUST control whether the registered system.control.* modules declare requires_approval (`setup.control_modules_declare_requires_approval`; 'partial' means some do and some do not). A driver that registers only annotated control modules cannot distinguish the corrected formula from the v1.15.0 one that shipped wrong."
  },
  "test_cases": [
    {
      "id": "no_system_modules",
      "note": "sys_modules.enabled=false \u2014 nothing registered, nothing to gate.",
      "setup": {
        "sys_modules": {
          "enabled": false
        },
        "strategy": "standard",
        "acl": null,
        "approval_handler": null,
        "policy": null,
        "control_modules_declare_requires_approval": false
      },
      "expected": {
        "control_modules_registered": false,
        "read_modules_registered": false,
        "acl_configured": false,
        "builtin_acl_gate_wired": true,
        "approval_handler_configured": false,
        "builtin_approval_gate_wired": true,
        "policy_strict": false,
        "all_control_modules_require_approval": false,
        "unprotected_control_surface": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "read_modules_only_no_acl",
      "note": "The 6 read modules with no ACL. An information-disclosure question, not a control-plane one \u2014 unprotected_control_surface MUST be false because there is no write surface at all.",
      "setup": {
        "sys_modules": {
          "enabled": true,
          "events": {
            "enabled": false
          }
        },
        "strategy": "standard",
        "acl": null,
        "approval_handler": null,
        "policy": null,
        "control_modules_declare_requires_approval": false
      },
      "expected": {
        "control_modules_registered": false,
        "read_modules_registered": true,
        "acl_configured": false,
        "builtin_acl_gate_wired": true,
        "approval_handler_configured": false,
        "builtin_approval_gate_wired": true,
        "policy_strict": false,
        "all_control_modules_require_approval": false,
        "unprotected_control_surface": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "control_modules_no_gates",
      "note": "All 9 registered, nothing attached. The condition the flag exists to report.",
      "setup": {
        "sys_modules": {
          "enabled": true,
          "events": {
            "enabled": true
          }
        },
        "strategy": "standard",
        "acl": null,
        "approval_handler": null,
        "policy": null,
        "control_modules_declare_requires_approval": true
      },
      "expected": {
        "control_modules_registered": true,
        "read_modules_registered": true,
        "acl_configured": false,
        "builtin_acl_gate_wired": true,
        "approval_handler_configured": false,
        "builtin_approval_gate_wired": true,
        "policy_strict": false,
        "all_control_modules_require_approval": true,
        "unprotected_control_surface": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "acl_configured_and_wired",
      "note": "ACL attached to an executor running `standard`, which contains acl_check.",
      "setup": {
        "sys_modules": {
          "enabled": true,
          "events": {
            "enabled": true
          }
        },
        "strategy": "standard",
        "acl": "attached",
        "approval_handler": null,
        "policy": null,
        "control_modules_declare_requires_approval": true
      },
      "expected": {
        "control_modules_registered": true,
        "read_modules_registered": true,
        "acl_configured": true,
        "builtin_acl_gate_wired": true,
        "approval_handler_configured": false,
        "builtin_approval_gate_wired": true,
        "policy_strict": false,
        "all_control_modules_require_approval": true,
        "unprotected_control_surface": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "acl_configured_but_strategy_has_no_step",
      "note": "The case that motivates the whole accessor: set_acl() on an executor running `internal`, which removes acl_check. acl_configured is true, builtin_acl_gate_wired is false, and the surface is unprotected. `acl != null` reports this as protected.",
      "setup": {
        "sys_modules": {
          "enabled": true,
          "events": {
            "enabled": true
          }
        },
        "strategy": "internal",
        "acl": "attached",
        "approval_handler": null,
        "policy": null,
        "control_modules_declare_requires_approval": true
